From a06f4f07f186a485b658c20f692bb78d9baddff9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 04:05:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] fix(backend): snapshots.csv never stays stale after an
 edit cut short

A label edit wrote state.json and then rebuilt the CSV; if the rebuild failed
(crash, full disk) the CSV kept the old label for good, since the check before
a download compared snapshot ids only, and PATCH answered 500 although the
label had changed.

- The check (ensure, and so the CSV download) compares every row with what the
  state.json files make now, so any difference, an edit cut short or a label
  edited by hand, rewrites the CSV.
- An edit marks the CSV stale (snapshots.csv.dirty) before it touches
  state.json; the marker goes when the CSV is next written, and while it is
  there the next capture rebuilds instead of appending.
- If the CSV cannot be rewritten once state.json has changed, the edit stands
  (PATCH answers 200 with the new label) and the marker stays for the next
  capture or download; if state.json itself cannot be written, nothing
  changes and PATCH fails as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
